// Request routing for the Mod Builder: classify a request as simple / standard /
// complex and pick the generation and repair models for it.
//
// Two classifiers (measured 2026-10-07, see docs "AI Mod Builder: tuning"):
//   haiku (default): one tiny Claude Haiku call that answers with a single word.
//     28 labelled eval prompts: 26/28; 12 held-out prompts: 11/12. ~$0.003 and
//     ~7 s per build. Falls back to the heuristic if the call fails.
//   heuristic: deterministic feature count over the request text. Free and
//     instant, 24/28 on the eval prompts it was tuned on but only 9/12 held out,
//     and its misses route too cheap (standard -> simple).
// Everything is configurable via env (read once at start):
//   MB_ROUTING            on (default) | off  (off = MB_MODEL for every call, the pre-tuning behaviour)
//   MB_CLASSIFIER         haiku (default) | heuristic
//   MB_MODEL_SIMPLE       default claude-sonnet-5-5
//   MB_MODEL_STANDARD     default claude-sonnet-5-5
